---
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/nine-hypotheses-identity-ladder-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/nine-hypotheses-identity-ladder-dark.svg?raw';
import Chart from './Chart.astro';
---

<Chart
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  title="Six rules, tried in order, decide whether two accounts are one person"
  caption="The first rule that matches wins. Only a fuzzy match can log a confidence under 0.9."
>
  Six matching rules in the order the resolver tries them, with the confidence it logs for each. Same account ID, same email and same normalized name each log 1.0. A known alias logs 0.95. The same first and last name logs 0.9. A fuzzy string match needs a score of 82 or more out of 100 and logs that score divided by 100, so it can land anywhere from 0.82 up. Any merge logged under 0.9 goes to a review list.
</Chart>
